  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting communities affected by HIV and TB in Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zambia has one of the world&apos;s worst HIV epidemics. One in seven adults is living with HIV, and about half of the people with HIV also have tuberculosis (TB). TB is responsible for more than a quarter of all HIV-related deaths in Zambia. People with HIV are vulnerable to TB because their immune systems are weak, but TB is often undetected and untreated in both people with and without HIV. This project will work with the government to link people with HIV and/or TB with health centres so that they are diagnosed and treated. Volunteers will teach people to recognise symptoms of HIV and TB and encourage them to seek health services. People with HIV and/or TB will be visited to help them adhere to their treatment. Family members of people with HIV and/or TB will be trained to provide care. The project will work with local health structures to make sure that support will continue when the grant ends. The project will work with other organisations to advocate for improved health services that respond to the needs of people with HIV and TB. As a result, more people will get better treatment for HIV and TB.</narrative>
  </description>
